        float64\n  RNETMIG2024              float64\n  RNETMIG2025              float64\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915331486},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I now understand the data:\n- farmers_markets table has a \"farmers_markets\" column (int64) and state information\n- census_data table has population estimates, with POPESTIMATE2025 being the 2025 population estimate\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Sum the total farmers markets\n2. Get the total U.S. population from census data (likely the U.S. total row)\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n\nFirst, let me peek at the data to understand the structure better - what's in the census data's NAME field that represents the U.S. total?","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I need to create a build script that joins these two datasets and computes the metric. Let me first peek at what row represents the U.S. total in the census data:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01J4kwvrad5PJcUbJ1eVs443","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"census_data","compose":"source.filter(source.SUMLEV == 10).select(\"NAME\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\").limit(5)"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":312,"cacheRead":19678,"cacheWrite":1550,"totalTokens":21554,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0015600000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0019678,"cacheWrite":0.0019375,"total":0.0054793},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":145},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915331487,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78Szp3pAR2EcUBr9MBr","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01J4kwvrad5PJcUbJ1eVs443","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"NAME\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n\"United States\",341784857\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915336617},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! So SUMLEV == 10 is the U.S. total, and the 2025 population is 341,784,857. Now I need to get the total farmers markets. Let me check that.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01HqhC8B8Ew6qP51hCSET72S","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.aggregate(total=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":168,"cacheRead":21228,"cacheWrite":350,"totalTokens":21759,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.00084,"cacheRead":0.0021228,"cacheWrite":0.0004375,"total":0.0034133},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":54},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915336617,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78TPFB9dbgisSeFZiv3","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01HqhC8B8Ew6qP51hCSET72S","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total\"\n7944\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915340053},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! So we have:\n- 7,944 total farmers markets\n- 341,784,857 U.S. population (2025)\n\nNow I need to create a build script that joins these two sources and calculates the metric. The metric should be: (7944 / 341784857) * 100000\n\nLet me create a build script for this cross-dataset metric.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a build script that joins both sources and calculates the metric:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01DQCYKkbFzxjiD7gV8GJUkV","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/private/tmp/trial-pi-86-63lir6pv/.xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_data\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Aggregate total farmers markets\ntotals = fact.aggregate(total_farmers_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get U.S. population (SUMLEV == 10 is the U.S. total)\nus_pop = (ref.filter(ref.SUMLEV == 10)\n          .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n          .mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and calculate the metric: farmers markets per 100,000 residents\nexpr = (\n    totals.join(us_pop, totals.k == us_pop.k)\n    .mutate(farmers_markets_per_100k=totals.total_farmers_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"farmers_markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":700,"cacheRead":21578,"cacheWrite":213,"totalTokens":22503,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0035,"cacheRead":0.0021578,"cacheWrite":0.00026625,"total":0.00593605},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":92},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915340053,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78TdUSFjmZruoy9uEUB","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01DQCYKkbFzxjiD7gV8GJUkV","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1275 bytes to /private/tmp/trial-pi-86-63lir6pv/.xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915346664},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me build this script and add it to the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01K9nPzo5o3tpmCZgmqtWdBz","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-86-6